In the diagram, $AC$ is parallel to $DG$, angle $BFG = 118^\circ$ and angle $ABE = 83^\circ$. Find the value of

(i) angle $CBF$;

(ii) $x$.

A trader is given a 15 percent discount on goods bought from a factory. If the original price of an item in the factory is ₵45,000,000.00, calculate

(i) the discount on the item;

(ii) the amount the trader paid for the item.

Using a ruler and a pair of compasses only,

(a) construct triangle $PQR$ such that the length of $PQ = 10$ cm, angle $QPR = 90^\circ$ and angle $PQR = 30^\circ$;

(b) measure the length of $PR$;

(c) bisect the angle $QRP$ to meet $PQ$ at $M$;

(d) with $M$ as centre and radius $MP$, draw a circle;

(e) measure the radius of the circle.

Type your measurements.
